# ML Core layer for macOS (Darwin)
# Platform-specific lockfile for deterministic pip-compile resolution.
#
# This file is macOS-specific because pip-compile cannot resolve
# conditional dependencies across platforms in a single graph.
#
# Run `make compile` in this directory to generate pinned ml-core-darwin.txt
#
# PLATFORM TARGET: darwin-* (macOS Intel + Apple Silicon)
#   - darwin-x86_64-cpu   (macOS Intel, DEPRECATED - see security note)
#   - darwin-arm64-cpu    (macOS Apple Silicon, CPU fallback)
#   - darwin-arm64-mps    (macOS Apple Silicon, Metal)
#
# SECURITY NOTE (CVE-2025-32434):
#   torch < 2.6.0 has a critical RCE vulnerability (CVSS 9.8) via torch.load()
#   - macOS Intel (x86_64): DEPRECATED - no torch 2.6.0+ wheels available from PyTorch
#   - macOS ARM64: uses torch 2.6.0+ (secure)
#
# See: requirements/README.md for layering rationale.

# --- PyTorch (macOS, security-aware) ---
# SECURITY: torch 2.6.0+ required to patch CVE-2025-32434 (torch.load RCE)
#
# macOS ARM64 (Apple Silicon): torch 2.6.0+ (secure, MPS support)
# macOS Intel (x86_64): NOT SUPPORTED - no official secure wheels available
#   Users must migrate to Apple Silicon or Linux for ML workloads.
#   (The parent ml-core.in excludes x86_64; this file only provides ARM64 packages.)
torch>=2.6.0,<3 ; platform_system == "Darwin" and platform_machine == "arm64"  # CVE-2025-32434 patched
torchvision>=0.21.0,<1 ; platform_system == "Darwin" and platform_machine == "arm64"  # matches torch 2.6.0+

